{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"alias":"hardshell-foldable-gourami","creation_channel":"python","description":"## Context / Problem\ndocs/architecture.md:537 says a seam \"is pinned by `tests/unit/test_prompt_model_module_seam.py`\". That module was deleted by commit 441ca94f4a8 (Gerrit 3050, story 3f35 of epic f400), so the sentence points at a file that no longer exists. Found by the epic f400 docs sweep (advisory T7): of 15 doc-referenced tests/scripts paths that no longer exist, this is the only one attributable to that epic.\n\n## Approach\nReword the sentence in docs/architecture.md so it no longer names the deleted module (state what now enforces the seam, or drop the clause if nothing does). Check with `git grep -n test_prompt_model_module_seam` that no other tracked file names it. The other 14 missing paths belong to other epics and are out of scope.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `git grep -n test_prompt_model_module_seam -- docs AGENTS.md CONTRIBUTING.md README.md` prints nothing, and `python scripts/check_docs_index.py --check` exits 0. Checked by running both commands on the change.\n","id":"0a13-be4f-18d0-4153","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Fix stale reference to deleted seam test in architecture.md"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793016911654270001,"uuid":"c72aab50-e97e-4f7d-a827-e502252cf223"}